---
description: Maestro canonical project rules — always apply
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and obey `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. It is the canonical, binding ruleset for
this project: hard boundaries (no paid or copyleft dependencies; the user owns git; no
secrets in code; design doc v15 is frozen — changes go through ADRs in `docs/adr/`), logic
placement (DB = invariants, Edge Functions = workflows/calculations, frontend = presentation
only), feature-first structure under `src/features/`, naming conventions (DB snake_case
plural tables, `timestamptz` only, RLS policy naming; TS strict, PascalCase components,
kebab-case files), security bar (deny-by-default RLS with `tenant_id` on every table in the
creating migration; adversarial pgTAP tests required for joint-project and portal paths;
append-only audit tables; signed URLs for media; Zod validation at every Edge Function
boundary), i18n/RTL from the first screen, and testing requirements.

Shared project memory is in `docs/memory/` — the same store every AI tool on this repository
reads and writes; there is no Cursor-specific memory. Start a task with
`docs/memory/README.md`, then `docs/memory/MAP.md` to find the one capsule that matters, then
the source it names. Never load the whole vault. Current source code beats any note: if they
disagree, fix the note. Write durable findings back (`traps.md`, `STATE.md`, the capsule) — but
a decision becomes an ADR, never a memory note. See `AGENTS.md` §9.

If any generated suggestion conflicts with `AGENTS.md`, follow `AGENTS.md`. Decisions that
change rules, stack, or schema shape require an ADR first. Reference `docs/TASKS.md` task IDs
in commit messages. Never commit or push — the user handles all git operations.
